{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["From his youth — from his early years, like בחרותיך. But therefore, 'upon his youth Adonai will not rejoice' — these are the men called בחורים." "Confine them — like: ויכלא הגשם. He bound them and restrained them from the market and placed them in the house of confinement. The alef-heh-ayin causes one to say כְּלַאֵם, like 'Adonai, we have heard,' 'he will find him in the desert land.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The second sentence quotes and interprets Hosea 9:10, where Rashbam connects the lemma's בחוריו to the wordplay with בחורים, 'young men.'", 1 "Rashbam cites the aleph-heh-ayin root pattern (א\"ה \"ע, using the abbreviation a\"ḥ h\"ʿ = אותיות ה\"ע, i.e., the letters heh-ayin) to explain the hifil form כלאם; the two supporting examples (שמענו אדני from Isaiah 26:8 and ימצאהו בארץ מדבר from Deut. 32:10) illustrate comparable hifil forms."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:01.884636424Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}